<title>ECUADOR: Ecuador's monetary base down 1.05 pct in Nov.</title>
<headline>Ecuador's monetary base down 1.05 pct in Nov.</headline>
<dateline>QUITO 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ecuador's monetary base fall 1.05 percent to 2.72 billion sucres in November, the Central Bank said Thursday.</p>
<p>In October, money base grew 7.46 percent to 2.75 billion sucres.</p>
<p>The bank did not give any reason for the increase.</p>
<p>The money base ended 1995 at 2.41 billion sucres, up from 1.85 billion sucres at the end of 1994.</p>
<p>--Gustavo Oviedo, Quito Newsroom, 5932 258433</p>
</text>
